      "field_name": "notes",
      "value": "First case report of aGCC-associated PNS. Amphiphysin-IgG positivity in both serum and CSF. Initial presentation was limbic encephalitis; recurrence 7 months later was paraneoplastic cerebellar dysfunction with head/trunk tremor, dysarthria, gait instability, gaze-evoked nystagmus, and cerebellar ataxia. Brain MRI showed mild cerebellar atrophy at recurrence. PET/CT showed no tumor metastasis. Immunohistochemistry of tumor tissue showed amphiphysin protein expression and CD3+, CD8+, CD20+ immune cell infiltration. Patient refused IVIG due to economic reasons.",
